WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
At school,

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.880
tests and grades are meant to show our progress

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.720
towards gaining practical skills

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.360
or understanding complicated ideas.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.760
Unfortunately, they often measure the wrong thing

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.160
or a limited form of progress.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.380
Albert Einstein said,

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.680
“Any fool can know. The point is to understand”.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.100
And he was right.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.040
There is no point in knowing what a solar panel is

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.260
if we don’t know why it was built or how to install it.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.080
Too often, tests focus on the what,

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.240
rather than the more important questions of

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.700
how or why.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.020
Multiple Choice is especially tricky.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.100
Governments and schools love it

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.060
because you can compute the results fast and cheap.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.460
Unfortunately, Multiple Choice

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.460
does not measure for creativity

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.280
or original thoughts.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.680
As long as test scores assess

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.420
only one very limited form of understanding,

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.340
there will be parents and teachers

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.160
that push children to focus on the wrong things:

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.840
facts for example.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.500
As long as kids have to study subjects

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.920
not aligned with their personal interest

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:08.840
- boredom,

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.240
confusion or low self-confidence will prevail.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.940
Psychologist Angela Duckworth says character,

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.640
perseverance and mindset

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.600
make all the difference in school,

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:21.980
work and life;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.140
she calls it ‘grit’.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.180
Famous neuroscientists Manfred Spitzer

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:30.440
argues the most important subjects to become

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.660
good at anything include music,

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.320
handcrafting, and drama,

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.040
which are difficult to measure with tests.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.500
Some top schools already focus on mindset

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.800
or teach theatre.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.100
In the west,

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.180
Montessori and Waldorf schools

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.340
help children to develop practical,

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.340
creative and social skills

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.480
whilst grades matter little.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:53.940
In East Asia,

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.880
there’s a new breed of Buddhists schools

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.480
that focus on character,

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:58.440
empathy,

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.620
awareness and mindset.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.220
What do you think?

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:06.760
Is it an accident that the visionary founders of Google,

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.040
Wikipedia and Amazon all went to Montessori,

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.140
a school that doesn't use grades?

